meta {
  name: Drools Spring App API
}

auth {
  mode: none
}

docs {
  Bruno collection for the `drools-spring-app` module.

  Business rules are defined as JSON, rendered to DRL and executed with Drools.

  Start the app first (port 8080):

      cd drools-spring-app && mvn spring-boot:run

  - "Test Business Rule" requests need no database.
  - "Create" / "Get" requests need MongoDB at mongodb://root:example@localhost:27017/admin.

  Select the "Local" environment. Running the whole collection works as a smoke test: every request
  has assertions. "Create Business Rule (example)" stores the created id in the businessRuleId variable.
}
